# ===========================================================================
#  AdaptaDrive - what is NOT tracked, and why
#
#  The rule: anything a reader needs to CHECK our claims is committed.
#  Anything that is large and can be regenerated by a documented command is
#  not. Every ignored item below names the command that rebuilds it.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Replay logs: ~4 GB, regenerate with run_experiments / finalize --------
# One SimLog holds the risk field, the 77-candidate fan and the predictions for
# every cycle of a run. A single intersection log is 273 MB. These drive the
# replay UI and the video renderer; they are not evidence for any number, since
# every metric is computed into results/runs.csv at the end of the run.
logs/
*.mat

# --- MATLAB / Simulink build artefacts -------------------------------------
slprj/
*.slxc
*.autosave
*.asv
*.m~
octave-workspace
codegen/

# --- Transient run logs ----------------------------------------------------
# Console output captured while running a batch. The CSVs are the record.
results/*.log

# --- Superseded measurements -----------------------------------------------
# Local backups of earlier matrices. Two runs.csv files with different numbers
# in one repository is an invitation to quote the wrong one; the before/after
# comparison that mattered is written up in docs/DEVIATIONS.md D29-D33.
results/archive_*/

# --- OS / editor cruft -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ===========================================================================
#  DELIBERATELY TRACKED, despite being generated
#  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#  results/*.csv          the measured evidence - every number in the README,
#                         RESULTS.md and STATUS.md comes from these
#  results/figures/*.png  the plots, each stamped with the CPU and MATLAB
#                         release it was measured on
#  results/stress/        the B5 stress-condition measurements
#  results/video/*.mp4    the demo video (10.6 MB), so the run can be watched
#                         without installing MATLAB
#  models/*.slx           the Stateflow behaviour chart, a deliverable
#
#  A results folder that is ignored is a project whose claims cannot be
#  checked without a MATLAB licence and four hours of compute.
# ===========================================================================
